WEBVTT

00:01.378 --> 00:04.897
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:04.933 --> 00:08.254
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:08.290 --> 00:11.869
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:11.905 --> 00:15.107
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:15.141 --> 00:18.110
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:18.144 --> 00:21.647
<i>Lucky there's a man
who positively can do</i>

00:21.681 --> 00:23.282
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:23.316 --> 00:25.017
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:25.051 --> 00:30.188
<i>He's... a... Fam... ily... Guy!</i>

00:37.163 --> 00:38.497
Happy birthday, Lois.

00:38.531 --> 00:40.799
You know, today you officially become

00:40.833 --> 00:42.634
the oldest woman I've ever slept with.

00:42.669 --> 00:44.803
Yes. You said the same thing last year.

00:44.837 --> 00:47.172
Well, unlike you,
that joke never gets old.

00:47.206 --> 00:49.241
Oh, and I forgot to pick up the cake.

00:49.275 --> 00:51.310
Hey, Lois, I don't like
any of these snacks.

00:51.344 --> 00:53.078
Can I have something from the kitchen?

00:53.112 --> 00:54.813
We can have snacks from the kitchen?

00:54.847 --> 00:56.248
I could go for a sandwich.

00:56.282 --> 00:58.650
No. No one gets snacks from the kitchen.

00:58.685 --> 01:00.719
You see what you started?

01:07.360 --> 01:08.994
Hi. I'm here for the pony rides.

01:09.028 --> 01:10.829
- What?
- Oh, boy.

01:10.863 --> 01:13.165
This-this must be
some sort of big mix-up.

01:13.199 --> 01:15.033
Don't worry, Lois, I'll handle this.

01:16.583 --> 01:18.403
- What's his name?
- Lightning.

01:18.438 --> 01:20.839
That means he's fast.

01:20.873 --> 01:22.374
So, uh, Lois, where are your parents?

01:22.408 --> 01:23.842
Didn't they say they were coming?

01:23.876 --> 01:26.712
Yeah, but I'm sure Daddy
had a last-minute work thing.

01:26.746 --> 01:28.680
He's always put business first.

01:28.715 --> 01:32.017
Even growing up, he never came
to any of my piano recitals.

01:32.051 --> 01:34.019
It was the '80s, so he was always doing

01:34.053 --> 01:36.521
cocaine-and-sushi business meetings.

01:36.556 --> 01:38.357
All right, Hideki, it's a deal.

01:38.391 --> 01:40.859
Now, let's celebrate
the way rich guys do, by...

01:42.395 --> 01:44.363
Ah, damn it, I snorted the wrong one.

01:44.397 --> 01:45.864
Ah, wasabi!

01:45.898 --> 01:47.799
Wasabi in my nostril!

01:49.435 --> 01:51.903
Still better than sitting
through that piano thing.

01:58.077 --> 02:00.579
Oh, hi, Daddy. You missed the party.

02:00.613 --> 02:02.481
I know. I thought I'd apologize

02:02.515 --> 02:04.950
with an upper-class
New England mumble-kiss.

02:06.419 --> 02:07.652
- I'm so sorry, dear.
- It's okay.

02:07.687 --> 02:09.621
And here, I brought you a gift.

02:11.081 --> 02:13.291
- A gun?
- Yeah, you love guns.

02:13.326 --> 02:14.993
No, I don't.

02:15.028 --> 02:16.661
You don't know me at all.

02:16.696 --> 02:18.730
I can't believe you'd blow off my party

02:18.765 --> 02:20.298
then give me a handgun.

02:20.333 --> 02:22.000
Especially when there's kids
in the house.

02:22.035 --> 02:23.235
<i>Hall. Kids in the Hall.</i>

02:23.269 --> 02:24.669
Damn it, Daddy.

02:24.704 --> 02:27.572
I'm trying to explain that guns
are hazardous and unsafe,

02:27.607 --> 02:29.107
not have a conversation about

02:29.142 --> 02:31.898
a tepid 1990s Canadian sketch group.

02:31.934 --> 02:33.512
You're wrong about guns and comedy.

02:33.546 --> 02:34.746
I'm out of here.

02:34.781 --> 02:36.081
Buh-bye.

02:36.115 --> 02:39.017
Was that a tepid 1990s
David Spade reference?

02:39.052 --> 02:41.386
People are allowed to like things!

02:44.957 --> 02:46.591
Peter, you want to watch Netflix?

02:46.626 --> 02:48.427
Yeah, let's watch one of those
stand-up specials.

02:48.461 --> 02:49.928
There's a bunch of 'em,
they got to be good.

02:50.662 --> 02:53.031
No. No.

02:53.066 --> 02:55.700
Tom Segura? No.

02:55.735 --> 02:57.369
Chinese girl.

02:57.403 --> 02:59.271
Another Chinese girl.

02:59.305 --> 03:01.206
No. No.

03:01.240 --> 03:02.707
Anjelah Johnson?

03:02.742 --> 03:04.109
Geez, they're giving one
of these to everyone.

03:04.143 --> 03:06.278
- How come I don't have one?
- You do, Peter.

03:06.312 --> 03:07.612
This is the taped intro.

03:07.647 --> 03:09.114
Mr. Griffin, you're on.

03:14.921 --> 03:18.223
Good evening, Ithaca Civic Auditorium.

03:19.725 --> 03:21.626
So I'm thinking I might get a bike.

03:23.329 --> 03:24.629
You know, one of these things?

03:24.664 --> 03:25.897
Ring-ring, ring-ring.

03:25.932 --> 03:28.400
"I'll get you, Toto!" Yeah.

03:28.434 --> 03:30.669
I'm thinking I might.

03:36.175 --> 03:38.543
Okay, I'm off to the grocery store.

03:38.578 --> 03:40.645
- So, what'd you do with the gun?
- Gun?

03:40.680 --> 03:43.915
Yeah, my father gave me a gun
as a present yesterday.

03:43.950 --> 03:45.750
Where was that during birthday sex?

03:45.785 --> 03:47.152
Maybe I would have finished.

03:47.186 --> 03:49.488
Unlike you, guns can actually fire.

03:49.522 --> 03:51.690
I don't think this marriage needs a gun.

03:51.724 --> 03:53.825
Anyway, I hid the gun someplace safe

03:53.860 --> 03:56.194
until I can figure out how to
properly dispose of it.

03:56.229 --> 03:58.697
So don't get any ideas.

03:58.731 --> 04:00.098
Good for Lois.

04:00.133 --> 04:01.666
Guns are a major problem,

04:01.701 --> 04:03.068
especially in the hands
of someone like...

04:04.737 --> 04:08.840
It was in a box with
Chris's adoption papers... Oh.

04:08.875 --> 04:11.443
You heard nothing.

04:14.547 --> 04:16.047
Hi, I got my gun here.

04:16.082 --> 04:17.549
I'd like to rent a stall, please.

04:17.583 --> 04:20.352
Sure. You need a tutorial
before you start?

04:20.386 --> 04:22.020
Yeah, it's a gun range.

04:22.054 --> 04:23.622
I think I got it.

04:24.724 --> 04:27.058
Wait! I think I did it wrong.

04:29.162 --> 04:31.263
So how was the gun range, Dad?

04:31.297 --> 04:33.398
Did you shoot up
that silhouette real good?

04:33.432 --> 04:38.036
That is so my dad.

04:42.742 --> 04:44.709
Now here to sing
the Heart classic "Alone"

04:44.744 --> 04:46.211
is Chris Griffin.

04:49.348 --> 04:52.217
<i>I hear the ticking of the clock</i>

04:52.251 --> 04:54.052
<i>I'm lying here</i>

04:54.086 --> 04:57.122
<i>The room's pitch dark</i>

05:00.126 --> 05:03.328
<i>I wonder where you are tonight</i>

05:03.362 --> 05:07.566
<i>No answer on the telephone.</i>

05:07.600 --> 05:09.768
Turn around.

05:11.938 --> 05:15.040
<i>We now return to The Orville on Fox.</i>

05:16.943 --> 05:19.344
Why do you hate that show so much?

05:19.378 --> 05:20.612
Because it's preventing me

05:20.646 --> 05:23.448
<i>from doing my work here at Family Guy.</i>

05:26.452 --> 05:29.154
Damn it, I think
I loaded a bullet wrong.

05:29.188 --> 05:31.223
All right, let's all take turns
looking down the barrel

05:31.257 --> 05:33.892
with one eyeball and see if we
can figure out what's going on.

05:33.926 --> 05:35.660
Chris, you go first.

05:35.695 --> 05:38.063
Oh, my God, Peter. Give me that.

05:38.097 --> 05:40.966
This gun is not staying in this
house for one more second.

05:41.000 --> 05:42.500
I'm giving it back to my father.

05:42.535 --> 05:44.069
Yeah, it's been a disaster.

05:44.103 --> 05:46.338
Like when Peter was the only one
not wearing black jeans

05:46.372 --> 05:47.772
at a Rush concert.

05:49.942 --> 05:51.576
Sing "Tom Sawyer"!

05:51.611 --> 05:53.011
We already did.

05:53.045 --> 05:54.446
And what are you wearing?!

05:54.480 --> 05:57.015
What? These are my concert khakis.

05:57.049 --> 05:59.618
Beat him! Beat him in six-eight time.

05:59.652 --> 06:01.353
And don't let him escape

06:01.387 --> 06:04.422
to the completely unoccupied
ladies' room.

06:04.457 --> 06:05.857
Ah! No. Please,

06:05.891 --> 06:08.627
uncles who voted for
Gary Johnson, leave me alone.

06:12.231 --> 06:15.967
And now a song about radio towers.

06:20.006 --> 06:21.640
Daddy?

06:21.674 --> 06:23.475
Daddy, are you there?

06:29.915 --> 06:31.783
Don't do anything to scare him.

06:31.817 --> 06:34.286
He flew on my shoulder
while I was having a lemonade.

06:34.320 --> 06:35.987
Daddy, I...

06:40.393 --> 06:41.526
What?

06:41.560 --> 06:43.228
Daddy, you need to take this gun back.

06:43.262 --> 06:45.230
I never should have accepted it
in the first place.

06:45.264 --> 06:46.865
And you never should have
given it to me.

06:46.899 --> 06:48.033
Are you sure?

06:48.067 --> 06:49.834
I bought it at Anthropologie.

06:49.869 --> 06:51.002
Oh.

06:51.037 --> 06:52.404
Wait a minute, what am I saying?

06:52.438 --> 06:53.872
No. You have to take it back.

06:53.906 --> 06:56.007
I'm not. You're keeping it. It's a gift.

06:56.042 --> 06:59.411
Damn it, Daddy, why won't you
just take the gun?

06:59.445 --> 07:01.646
Oh, my God! Daddy!

07:01.681 --> 07:02.881
I'm so sorry.

07:02.915 --> 07:04.482
It can't be too serious.

07:04.517 --> 07:07.018
They haven't done an overhead
crane shot yet.

07:07.053 --> 07:09.154
Oh, God! There it is!

07:09.188 --> 07:11.156
I'm calling 911.

07:11.190 --> 07:13.191
Oh, no. It's floating up,

07:13.225 --> 07:15.727
signifying his spirit leaving his body.

07:17.463 --> 07:19.597
And there's the single minor key note.

07:19.632 --> 07:20.999
This is bad.

07:21.033 --> 07:24.369
<i>Family Guy will be right back.</i>

07:24.403 --> 07:26.871
Well, now it doesn't seem so serious.

07:35.057 --> 07:37.191
Hey, quick question:
any of you guys know how

07:37.225 --> 07:38.793
to countersue somebody?

07:38.827 --> 07:41.095
Dr. Hartman, please, how's my father?

07:41.129 --> 07:43.030
Well, at this point, it's hard to say.

07:43.065 --> 07:44.899
He suffered severe head trauma.

07:44.933 --> 07:46.967
<i>So if you want to beat him
in Mario Kart,</i>

07:47.002 --> 07:48.536
this is your chance.

07:51.406 --> 07:54.909
And the champ is dethroned.

07:56.478 --> 07:58.813
Oh, poor Daddy. You know what?

07:58.847 --> 08:00.715
We're gonna bring him home with us

08:00.749 --> 08:03.417
and take care of him until he's 100%.

08:03.452 --> 08:05.052
What? Oh, come on, Mom.

08:05.087 --> 08:07.755
I want Grandpa to get better,
too, but living with us?

08:07.789 --> 08:09.557
Why can't Grandma take care of him?

08:09.591 --> 08:10.758
Oh, she's busy.

08:10.792 --> 08:12.727
She went to Antarctica
to steal a penguin.

08:12.761 --> 08:14.061
Penguin?

08:14.096 --> 08:16.831
Daddy's gonna require
all our love and support.

08:16.865 --> 08:18.499
Well, you got the right guy for that.

08:18.533 --> 08:20.067
I'm great at supporting people.

08:20.102 --> 08:23.337
<i>On Mad Men,
I was Christina Hendricks' bra.</i>

08:23.372 --> 08:25.239
Joan, can you call a meeting
of the partners?

08:25.273 --> 08:26.440
Help me.

08:26.475 --> 08:29.009
Too much is being asked of me.

08:29.044 --> 08:30.311
At least you're there.

08:30.345 --> 08:32.480
I'm Jon Hamm's underwear.

08:32.514 --> 08:34.482
Why am I Elisabeth Moss's socks?

08:34.516 --> 08:36.083
Chris and I should switch.

08:36.118 --> 08:38.619
- Yeah, let's switch.
- We're gonna switch.

08:42.657 --> 08:44.191
All right, Chris,
give me a hand with Carter.

08:48.230 --> 08:49.964
Hey, I heard another chair.

08:50.999 --> 08:53.100
Oh, my God, oh, my God, oh, my God!

08:53.135 --> 08:55.836
He's not paralyzed, Joe,
he's just recovering.

08:55.871 --> 08:57.471
Ah.

09:01.143 --> 09:04.044
All right, Daddy living here
is gonna be a big adjustment,

09:04.079 --> 09:06.447
and we're all gonna
have to make sacrifices.

09:06.481 --> 09:08.883
So, Meg, Daddy will sleep in your room,

09:08.917 --> 09:11.285
and Stewie and Chris,
you'll stay where you are.

09:11.319 --> 09:13.788
What? I'm the only one sacrificing.

09:13.822 --> 09:16.290
Don't be ridiculous, Meg.
I said everybody's names.

09:16.324 --> 09:18.526
Come on, Meg, it won't be any
worse than when I took

09:18.560 --> 09:20.895
GГ©rard Depardieu to Burning Man.

09:20.929 --> 09:22.329
I feel so free.

09:22.364 --> 09:23.864
My breasts are muddied up.

09:23.899 --> 09:25.900
I'm tripping balls.

09:25.934 --> 09:28.502
Easy, GГ©rard, we're still
at Enterprise Rent-A-Car.

09:28.537 --> 09:30.137
I'm gonna go crazy.

09:30.172 --> 09:31.872
You can poop anywhere.

09:31.907 --> 09:34.175
We'll take the insurance.

09:37.045 --> 09:39.313
All right, Carter, now we're
gonna try and jog your memory

09:39.347 --> 09:41.382
and get you talking
with some familiar pictures.

09:41.417 --> 09:43.925
So, I will hold them up
and you say what they are.

09:44.553 --> 09:47.087
What? You don't know who this is?

09:47.122 --> 09:48.889
<i>But he's so talented.</i>

09:48.924 --> 09:50.157
Anyone who doesn't know who he is

09:50.192 --> 09:52.259
brings shame on his children and wife.

09:52.294 --> 09:54.328
Peter, come on.
We're trying to help Daddy,

09:54.362 --> 09:57.498
not relive our embarrassing loss
to Joe and Bonnie in Celebrity.

09:57.532 --> 09:59.099
All right, fine. Next picture.

09:59.134 --> 10:02.336
What? You don't know who he is, either?

10:02.370 --> 10:04.438
Go on, Lois, scream at him
that he should know.

10:04.473 --> 10:06.340
This guy was in a movie once.

10:06.374 --> 10:09.009
That means we need to put a
fifth head on Mount Rushmore.

10:09.044 --> 10:11.011
Damn it, Peter, you should've
known who he is.

10:11.046 --> 10:12.680
Even Joe knew.

10:12.714 --> 10:15.015
Yep, Joe sure did.

10:15.050 --> 10:17.284
Hey, Ansel Elgort and Gemma Arterton

10:17.319 --> 10:19.086
are in a Cary Fukunaga film.

10:19.120 --> 10:20.888
Good for them.

10:23.592 --> 10:26.293
<i>All right, Daddy, I know NCIS is on,</i>

10:26.328 --> 10:28.696
<i>but I want to watch Real Housewives,</i>

10:28.730 --> 10:31.198
unless you tell me not to.

10:33.268 --> 10:34.869
Oh, those two hate each other.

10:34.903 --> 10:36.904
These two have a three-year-old feud

10:36.938 --> 10:40.040
based on an offhanded remark
at a charity fashion show.

10:42.444 --> 10:44.745
I'm sure Andy Cohen will explain it all

10:44.779 --> 10:47.214
<i>on Watch What Happens Live
after the show.</i>

10:47.249 --> 10:50.050
No! The show itself is bad enough!

10:50.085 --> 10:52.920
We don't need another show
explaining what we just saw.

10:52.954 --> 10:54.555
Daddy! You're back.

10:54.589 --> 10:56.490
Please, anything but this show.

10:56.525 --> 10:58.559
We could watch Netflix.

10:58.593 --> 11:00.427
<i>Uh, Cleveland Brown:</i>

11:00.462 --> 11:03.097
<i>You Startin' To See What I'm Sayin'?</i>

11:03.131 --> 11:04.999
So, the president pulls the plug

11:05.033 --> 11:07.434
on an investigation into the president?

11:07.469 --> 11:09.470
You startin' to see what I'm sayin'?

11:16.545 --> 11:18.479
Since you're doing
a little better, Daddy,

11:18.513 --> 11:20.347
I thought you should see where you work.

11:20.382 --> 11:23.150
It might help trigger
more memories about your life.

11:23.184 --> 11:26.287
I work here? Wow. This place is huge.

11:26.321 --> 11:27.855
What do we do? Are we nice?

11:27.889 --> 11:30.090
You put pesticides in baby food.

11:30.125 --> 11:32.682
- Aw.
- Not only that, your chemical waste

11:32.718 --> 11:34.695
- gave a town cancer.
- Yikes.

11:34.729 --> 11:37.385
You burned down
the entire Amazon rain forest.

11:37.420 --> 11:39.190
- Whoops
- You're the number-one producer

11:39.226 --> 11:40.467
- of whale meat.
- Sheesh.

11:40.502 --> 11:42.903
- You dumped lead in drinking water.
- Zoinks.

11:42.939 --> 11:45.773
Your oil pipeline moved
12 Native American tribes.

11:45.807 --> 11:48.542
Your fertilizer plant exploded,

11:48.577 --> 11:50.611
killing 4,000.

11:50.645 --> 11:53.447
- You bought Vine and shut it down.
- I did what?

11:53.481 --> 11:56.183
- You bought Vine and shut it down.
- I did what?

11:56.217 --> 11:58.986
- You bought Vine and shut it down.
- I did what?

11:59.020 --> 12:01.722
I'm sorry, Daddy, but you're
a very cutthroat businessman.

12:01.756 --> 12:02.957
And maybe worst of all,

12:02.991 --> 12:06.193
you engage in constant,
gratuitous animal testing.

12:06.227 --> 12:08.862
<i>Sir, as you requested, we had
all the monkeys watch Vikings.</i>

12:08.897 --> 12:10.731
Did they like it?
Do they think it's worth

12:10.765 --> 12:12.466
- me putting in the time?
- Uh, no.

12:12.500 --> 12:13.968
- They didn't care for it.
- Good.

12:14.002 --> 12:15.202
This is valuable information.

12:15.236 --> 12:17.204
Now have them watch Sarah Jessica Parker

12:17.238 --> 12:19.239
<i>and Thomas Haden Church in Divorce.</i>

12:19.274 --> 12:22.977
<i>Sir, they've just watched
66 consecutive hours of Vikings.</i>

12:23.011 --> 12:24.144
- If you could...
- Oh, what, so you want humans

12:24.179 --> 12:25.646
<i>to watch Divorce?</i>

12:25.680 --> 12:28.349
Because if monkeys don't,
that's what has to happen.

12:28.383 --> 12:31.251
Wow, I guess I was
a cutthroat businessman.

12:31.286 --> 12:33.087
But what about when I wasn't at work?

12:33.121 --> 12:34.321
What did we do together?

12:34.356 --> 12:36.156
Well, sometimes you made me reenact

12:36.191 --> 12:39.259
<i>Kids in the Hall sketches
that basically had no endings.</i>

12:45.066 --> 12:47.401
But to be honest, we didn't do much.

12:47.435 --> 12:49.870
- Your work always came first.
- Really?

12:49.904 --> 12:52.840
And you still took care of me
when I was hurt?

12:52.874 --> 12:55.676
I... I don't like who I was.

12:55.710 --> 12:59.246
But from now on, I'm going to be
a better father and grandfather.

12:59.280 --> 13:01.548
We're going to spend real time together.

13:01.583 --> 13:04.284
Really? Oh, that'd be wonderful.

13:04.319 --> 13:07.688
I haven't been this happy
since I went on Safari.

13:07.722 --> 13:10.424
Oh, my God. This is so much
faster than Firefox.

13:10.458 --> 13:13.027
All right, let me go to Facebook.

13:13.061 --> 13:16.030
F-A...

13:16.064 --> 13:18.966
It's auto filling "Fat Butt Rodeo"?

13:19.000 --> 13:20.534
Peter!

13:20.568 --> 13:23.570
You were supposed to stay on Firefox.

13:29.611 --> 13:32.212
Morning, pumpkin. I brought muffins.

13:32.247 --> 13:33.414
You brought pumpkin muffins?

13:33.448 --> 13:36.324
- What? No. Wh-What?
- But you said...

13:36.360 --> 13:37.584
You know what?
Let's try it one more time.

13:37.619 --> 13:39.887
Hey, sweetie pie. I brought muffins.

13:39.921 --> 13:42.489
- You brought sweet pies and muffins?
- No.

13:44.192 --> 13:45.392
We've already done that.

13:45.427 --> 13:47.094
Damn it, now it's gonna go back outside.

13:49.531 --> 13:51.899
Wow, Daddy,
you really meant what you said.

13:51.933 --> 13:55.102
It's been wonderful spending
so much quality time with you.

13:55.136 --> 13:57.438
Yeah, Carter. You know, you've
always been a real bastard,

13:57.472 --> 13:59.773
but I got to say, it's nice to
see you turning things around.

13:59.808 --> 14:01.909
Thanks. You know,
you guys made me realize

14:01.943 --> 14:04.411
that I wasted my whole life
caring about money,

14:04.446 --> 14:06.613
and I'm not giving up another second.

14:06.648 --> 14:07.781
That's why I've decided

14:07.816 --> 14:09.583
to retire from Pewterschmidt Industries

14:09.617 --> 14:11.785
and give all my money to charity.

14:11.820 --> 14:13.987
Oh, Daddy, that's wonderful.

14:14.022 --> 14:15.489
Yeah, Carter. Good for you.

14:15.523 --> 14:17.591
Thanks. You know, I was a little worried

14:17.625 --> 14:19.760
you guys would be mad
about losing your inheritance.

14:19.794 --> 14:21.428
Oh, Daddy, I don't care.

14:21.463 --> 14:23.197
I've seen what wealth's done to you,

14:23.231 --> 14:25.265
and I certainly don't want that
to happen to us.

14:25.300 --> 14:27.367
Besides, we're regular people.

14:27.402 --> 14:30.771
We wouldn't miss millions
of dollars, right, Peter?

14:30.805 --> 14:32.806
I'm thinking I might.

14:41.049 --> 14:43.550
So, it's weird being Japanese.

14:43.585 --> 14:46.854
Last night, my husband wanted 69.

14:46.888 --> 14:50.023
I said, "Why do you want
beef and broccoli now?"

14:50.058 --> 14:53.160
<i>Hey, that's Chinese.</i>

14:59.657 --> 15:02.159
Look, I know you're upset
about losing our inheritance,

15:02.193 --> 15:04.495
but when we got married,
the first thing I told you

15:04.529 --> 15:06.230
is I didn't want Daddy's money.

15:06.264 --> 15:07.464
Well, yeah, not now,

15:07.499 --> 15:08.966
but I didn't know you meant forever.

15:09.000 --> 15:11.135
Peter, stop being so selfish.

15:11.169 --> 15:13.971
For the first time in my life,
I have a father who's kind

15:14.005 --> 15:16.006
and wants to spend time with me.

15:16.040 --> 15:18.642
And that's more important
than any inheritance.

15:18.676 --> 15:20.177
Yeah, well, I still want that money.

15:20.211 --> 15:22.146
It's the only way
I can afford that surgery

15:22.180 --> 15:25.182
to turn myself into 100% stained glass.

15:26.551 --> 15:28.852
- I don't get it.
- Neither do I.

15:31.222 --> 15:33.824
Oh, my God.

15:33.858 --> 15:35.692
Dad's beautiful.

15:38.196 --> 15:39.897
All right, guys. Now, the way I see it,

15:39.931 --> 15:42.432
Carter's only giving away
his money 'cause he's nice now.

15:42.467 --> 15:43.834
So to get our inheritance,

15:43.868 --> 15:46.336
we have to figure out a way
to make him mean again.

15:46.371 --> 15:48.839
I don't know, Dad.
He seems pretty happy.

15:48.873 --> 15:51.675
Anyone can get mad, Chris.
Even Shaquille O'Neal.

15:51.709 --> 15:53.177
Excuse me.

15:53.211 --> 15:56.246
My flapjacks was supposed
to have a Superman "S" on them.

15:56.281 --> 15:59.616
Are you mad? I...
I can't tell if you're mad.

15:59.651 --> 16:01.518
Very mad. This is unacceptable.

16:01.553 --> 16:03.253
At's the point
of having millions of dollars

16:03.288 --> 16:04.888
if everything can't be Superman?

16:04.923 --> 16:07.357
Okay, well, we'll fix it right away.

16:07.392 --> 16:09.026
Is there anything else I can get you?

16:09.060 --> 16:10.460
Yes. A big ambulance.

16:10.495 --> 16:12.863
I am stuck in this booth.

16:12.897 --> 16:15.432
So, ideas... how do we
make Carter mean again?

16:15.466 --> 16:16.867
Why don't we hire a prostitute

16:16.901 --> 16:19.069
to bring him almost to completion?

16:19.103 --> 16:22.372
Okay, don't love that my daughter
came out of the gates with that.

16:22.407 --> 16:24.875
Why don't we just mix up
all the colors of his Play-Doh?

16:24.909 --> 16:26.877
<i>Chris.</i>

16:26.911 --> 16:28.712
Well, you know what gets
Gargamel all riled up

16:28.746 --> 16:31.148
is those pesky Smurfs.
Maybe there's something there.

16:31.182 --> 16:32.883
Ooh, I know, I know.

16:32.917 --> 16:35.552
Why don't we hire a transvestite
to pick him up at a bar,

16:35.587 --> 16:36.987
then take off her wig

16:37.021 --> 16:38.488
at the exact moment of completion?

16:38.523 --> 16:39.890
Yeah, Meg, take it down a notch.

16:39.924 --> 16:41.225
I know what'll make him mad.

16:41.259 --> 16:43.393
Let's get him a book for Christmas.

16:43.428 --> 16:45.329
Didn't I get you all books
for Christmas?

16:45.363 --> 16:48.232
Yeah. And now I've got something
for you to read, genius.

16:48.266 --> 16:51.235
It's called the room.

16:51.269 --> 16:53.737
Hey, wait, I got something.
How do we summon Zuul?

16:53.771 --> 16:55.239
I bet Zuul could help.

16:55.273 --> 16:57.307
Why don't we take him
to a truck stop bathroom,

16:57.342 --> 16:58.909
and then after completion, we...

16:58.943 --> 17:00.844
Okay, Meg, are you trying
to get a rise out of me?

17:00.879 --> 17:02.279
'Cause guess what, young lady?

17:02.313 --> 17:04.114
It worked.

17:04.148 --> 17:06.250
Well, at least I'm saying real ideas

17:06.284 --> 17:07.417
and not just repeating things

17:07.452 --> 17:09.086
I've seen in children's programming.

17:09.120 --> 17:11.255
Yeah, Dad, I kind of agree with Meg.

17:11.289 --> 17:14.024
It seems like you're going
for comedy over substance.

17:14.058 --> 17:16.093
I see. Well, then,

17:16.127 --> 17:18.629
I have one last idea
how to make Carter mean.

17:18.663 --> 17:20.931
Turn him into one of my kids.

17:27.972 --> 17:29.873
So, what do you want to do today?

17:29.908 --> 17:31.441
You know, this may be crazy,

17:31.476 --> 17:34.611
but I'd love to finally
play piano for you.

17:34.646 --> 17:36.713
Cool, like Alicia Keys.

17:36.748 --> 17:39.449
A piano player named Keys?

17:39.484 --> 17:42.719
- That has to be fake, right?
- Yeah, I'd think so.

17:42.754 --> 17:44.955
That's pretty dumb.
I mean, if I was in a band,

17:44.989 --> 17:46.990
I wouldn't call myself Carter Guitar.

17:47.025 --> 17:48.292
I know, right?

17:48.326 --> 17:50.060
Actually, I like Carter Guitar.

17:50.094 --> 17:52.496
- I want to be that now.
- Hey, I have an idea.

17:52.530 --> 17:53.897
Why don't we do something together?

17:53.932 --> 17:55.632
I'll play, and you sing.

17:55.667 --> 17:57.801
Sounds great.
Who's the guy who married a kid

17:57.835 --> 17:59.303
and then later on killed his wife?

17:59.337 --> 18:01.238
- Jerry Lee Lewis.
- That's it.

18:01.272 --> 18:04.808
<i>You shake my nerves
and you rattle my brain</i>

18:04.842 --> 18:07.711
<i>Something, some-something,
something, something insane</i>

18:07.745 --> 18:10.480
<i>Goodness gracious, great balls of fire</i>

18:12.083 --> 18:14.051
Y-You don't have to sing the piano part.

18:14.085 --> 18:15.419
I'm playing it.

18:15.453 --> 18:17.321
All right, here's the plan.

18:17.355 --> 18:18.822
I clothespin his balls.

18:18.856 --> 18:21.758
Meg and Chris, you twist his
nipples in opposite directions.

18:21.793 --> 18:23.226
I'm glad you came around.

18:23.261 --> 18:25.729
Peter, you may want
to take a look at this.

18:25.763 --> 18:29.166
<i>You shake my nerves
and you rattle my brain...</i>

18:29.200 --> 18:31.435
Oh, my God. Look at them.

18:31.469 --> 18:34.171
This is just what
she's been saying she wanted:

18:34.205 --> 18:38.008
to spend time with her dad
and for him to love her.

18:38.042 --> 18:41.511
I guess that really is
more important than money.

18:41.546 --> 18:44.014
Wow. Dad's really taking this to heart.

18:44.048 --> 18:46.116
Meg. Meg.

18:46.150 --> 18:47.851
Tie my shoe.

18:47.885 --> 18:50.454
Hey, let's do another.
How about my karaoke song?

18:50.488 --> 18:51.855
Sure, what-what is it?

18:51.889 --> 18:53.690
<i>The theme to Hill Street Blues.</i>

18:53.725 --> 18:55.525
What? But that doesn't have any lyrics.

18:55.560 --> 18:57.227
The hell it doesn't.

18:57.261 --> 19:01.465
<i>Hill Street blues, Hill Street blues</i>

19:01.499 --> 19:03.367
<i>Hill Street blues</i>

19:03.401 --> 19:06.036
<i>I've got those Hill Street blues.</i>

19:06.070 --> 19:07.871
Wow, you're good.

19:07.905 --> 19:10.574
Of course I'm good. I'm Carter Guitar.

19:10.608 --> 19:15.078
<i>Hill Street blues, Hill Street blues</i>

19:15.113 --> 19:16.980
<i>Hill Street blues</i>

19:17.015 --> 19:19.716
<i>I've got those Hill Street blues</i>

19:19.751 --> 19:22.252
There were some ugly people
on that show.

19:22.286 --> 19:24.554
That's what made it real.

19:24.589 --> 19:26.990
<i>Hill Street blues</i>

19:27.025 --> 19:30.660
<i>Hill Street blues, Hill Streeblues</i>

19:30.695 --> 19:33.930
<i>I've got those Hill Street blues.</i>

19:33.965 --> 19:35.932
What are you doing here?

19:35.967 --> 19:38.235
I'm sorry I only cared
about the money, Lois.

19:38.269 --> 19:41.772
You were right. You having
a dad is way more important.

19:41.806 --> 19:44.107
Thanks, Peter.

19:46.110 --> 19:50.747
<i>Hill Street blues, Hill Street blues</i>

19:50.782 --> 19:52.416
<i>Hill Street blues...</i>

19:52.450 --> 19:55.585
Oh, my God! Daddy!

19:55.620 --> 19:59.189
Who told Carter he could
give away our (BLEEP) money?

20:05.948 --> 20:09.043
Daddy? Daddy, please tell me
you can hear me.

20:09.079 --> 20:11.848
Wh-Wha... What's going on?

20:11.882 --> 20:13.716
And what are you idiots doing here?

20:13.750 --> 20:16.686
I can't waste time with you.
I'm a cutthroat businessman.

20:16.720 --> 20:18.855
Aw, the gunshot changed him back.

20:18.889 --> 20:22.391
Oh, thank God. There's my Carter.

20:22.426 --> 20:23.860
Well, I guess it was nice

20:23.894 --> 20:25.695
to have time with Daddy while I could.

20:25.729 --> 20:27.864
And Peter, I'm glad you filly realized

20:27.898 --> 20:30.032
family is more important than money.

20:30.067 --> 20:31.300
Me too, Lois.

20:31.335 --> 20:32.702
And I think we all learned

20:32.736 --> 20:34.871
a valuable lesson about firearms.

20:34.905 --> 20:37.807
That's right, Peter.
Guns create problems,

20:37.841 --> 20:39.809
but they solve them, too.

20:39.843 --> 20:42.378
You said it, Lois.
And you know who else has a gun?

20:42.412 --> 20:45.214
Stan Smith. Take it away, Stan.

20:45.249 --> 20:46.549
Peter, that's...

20:46.583 --> 20:48.251
that show's not on after us anymore.

20:48.285 --> 20:50.086
Oh. What is on?

20:50.120 --> 20:53.122
Something as or more successful?

20:59.898 --> 21:03.429
Thank you for watching "Family Guy" on
www.FOX-fan.tv